From: Kaloyan Naumov <knaumov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:16:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0007-b70-ple-fp8-pinned-table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

L2 PLE n-gram table in FP8 (Lumnus-own, NOT from wu1ff) — halves the steady pinned host RAM (~95.4 -> ~47.7 GiB)

Purpose:  Keep the static PLE n-gram table as FP8 E4M3 in the XPU pinned slabs (1 B/value instead of BF16's 2)
          and dequantise only the looked-up rows. The table + its single global scale come from a .safetensors
          file cut from Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8@236dfdf2 (B70_PLE_FP8_PATH); the served weights stay W4A16.
          The FP8 storage/lookup/dequant path already exists upstream (Qwen4ExpPLEFp8EmbeddingMethod, the
          dtype-preserving pinned lookup, raw-byte ETP all-reduce, Qwen4ExpPLELayer._dequantize_embeddings after
          the gather) — it was just never selectable for a W4A16 checkpoint with an external table. This patch:
            * B70_PLE_FP8=1 forces the FP8 PLE method (subclass B70PLEFp8PinnedEmbeddingMethod) + pinned storage;
            * loads B70_PLE_FP8_PATH by zero-copy mmap straight into the FP8 pinned slabs (0006-style, no pageable
              copy), accepting either a 'table' tensor or the checkpoint's own '...shard_<i>.weight' keys, plus
              exactly one 'weight_scale'; refuses to start on any dtype/shape/row-count/scale mismatch;
            * when PLE_TABLE_PATH (the BF16 table) is still set, cross-checks 4096 random rows (relative L2 error,
              refuses above B70_PLE_FP8_MAX_REL_ERR, default 0.25; B70_PLE_FP8_CROSSCHECK=0 skips it);
            * maps only tensors of known dtypes (I64/BOOL/float/int mapped; unknown dtypes skipped), so extra keys
              in the file are ignored; if the file carries ngram_heads_offsets / ngram_heads_vocab_sizes /
              layer_multipliers they must equal the model's buffers (else refuse: different hash layout);
            * moves FP8 as bytes everywhere on XPU (uint8 UVA views for the Triton gather, byte copy in finalize),
              and dequantises with a 256-entry code LUT (value x scale in fp32, then one rounding) — bitwise equal
              to the stock cast-and-multiply; B70_PLE_FP8_DEQUANT=cast selects the stock cast instead.
          Default OFF: with B70_PLE_FP8 unset every code path is 0006's/wu1ff's, unchanged.
Depends:  0002 (pinned slabs), 0006 (direct-pinned fill; this patch sits on 0006's result).
Base:     vLLM v0.30.0 (ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607) after 0001-0006, i.e. sha256
          d28c99b19e077d549e581015569cf604aadcac32f0cef30a2c9c3e2b7ae0f116 (B70-0006).
          Result: sha256 5251494c662fbc1d403d1641be5f3b12783518b49bde5fa1bdaa009b4cdaee4e (verify-overlay.sh prints "B70-0007").
Rev 2:    2026-09-28 — first live boot refused our FP8 table file on its I64 layout tensors (unsupported dtype);
          the reader now maps/skips them. Checked against the real file on the model volume: 132 tensors, 128 shards,
          scale 1.99318e-4, layout equal, cross-check rel err 0.0266.
Origin:   Lumnus.
Method:   diff -u against the post-0006 file read from the running pod; chain-checked from upstream with
          patch --fuzz=0; CPU unit test of the real patched functions.
Apply:    patch -p1 --fuzz=0 from the directory that CONTAINS vllm/ (site-packages AND /workspace/vllm), after 0006.
